/*! \mainpage i-Telex firmware
 *
 * This is the generated source documentation for the i-Telex **module
 * firmware**: the code that runs on the Ethernet card of an i-Telex system and
 * carries teleprinter traffic over IP.
 *
 * The firmware is Fred Sonnenrein's work. This repository is a clone of his
 * SourceForge SVN project, kept so that the work is preserved and stays
 * buildable with current tools; the portable build, the tests and this
 * documentation are maintenance around it and do not change its provenance.
 * Most of the source comments are in German, as written by their authors.
 *
 * \section mainpage_what What the firmware does
 *
 * An i-Telex system connects a teleprinter to the i-Telex network over the
 * Internet. The module firmware documented here answers and places calls,
 * converts between the teleprinter's Baudot/ITA2 characters and the network
 * protocol, queries the subscriber directory server, serves the card's own web
 * configuration pages, and drives the other cards of the system over the
 * backplane.
 *
 * Two variants are built from these sources:
 *
 * - **Standard**, an ATmega2561 with external SRAM and an optional SD card;
 * - **Light**, an ATmega1284P without external memory, which compiles out the
 *   SD card, the shell and Telnet server, e-mail, and two of the four
 *   interface languages.
 *
 * The i-Telex functions themselves are identical on both.
 *
 * \section mainpage_layout Finding your way around
 *
 * - \b iTelex/ is the i-Telex application itself, and is where to start
 *   reading. `iTelex.c` holds the call state machine, `TlnBuch.c` and
 *   `TlnServer.c` the local subscriber book and the directory server client,
 *   `Protokoll.c` the i-Telex network protocol, `StringTab.h` the
 *   multilingual interface strings, and `IspMaster.c` the ISP programming of
 *   the system's other cards.
 * - \b system/, \b hardware/ and \b apps/ are the supporting embedded stack —
 *   the IP stack, the ENC28J60 driver, timers, the HTTP server and the shell.
 *   They come from Dirk Broßwick's AVR mini webserver project, whose original
 *   introduction is kept at \subpage mikrowebserver.
 * - \b Gemeinsam/ holds the sources shared with the other i-Telex cards,
 *   including the Baudot code tables, the backplane communication and the ring
 *   buffer. They live in the separate `itelex-misc` repository and are
 *   documented here because the module firmware compiles them in.
 * - \b FastBoot/ is Peter Dannegger's bootloader, which allows the card to be
 *   reprogrammed over its serial port.
 *
 * The line interface cards — TW39, ED1000, the analogue modem and the rest —
 * run their own firmware from `itelex-misc` rather than this code. The module
 * programs them over the backplane by ISP.
 *
 * \section mainpage_more Beyond the source
 *
 * Build instructions, the firmware variants, the host unit tests and the
 * dependency notes are in the repository's `README.md`. The project's
 * inherited German notes, the manual test plan, the per-build changelog and
 * the protocol captures are under `docs/`.
 *
 * The hardware itself is described on the
 * <a href="https://www.i-telex.net/hardware/">i-Telex hardware page</a>.
 */
